# 詞： 銀包

1. 我唔見咗個銀包，入面有身份證同信用卡。 (I lost my wallet. There's my ID card and credit cards inside.)

2. 你可唔可以借個銀包我睇吓，我想睇吓你張新卡。 (Can you lend me your wallet to take a look? I want to see your new card.)

3. 佢成日都唔記得帶銀包出街，每次都要我幫佢找數。 (He always forgets to bring his wallet when going out, and I have to pay for him every time.)

4. 呢個銀包係我阿媽送嘅生日禮物，我用咗好多年都唔捨得換。 (This wallet was a birthday gift from my mom. I've used it for many years and can't bear to replace it.)

5. 小心啲呀，呢區好多扒手，睇住你個銀包呀！ (Be careful! There are many pickpockets in this area. Watch your wallet!)

6. 佢個銀包脹卜卜，一定係啱啱出咗糧。 (His wallet is bulging. He must have just gotten paid.)

7. 我喺街上執到個銀包，交咗畀警察處理。 (I picked up a wallet on the street and handed it over to the police.)

8. 而家好多人用手機支付，帶銀包出街嘅人越嚟越少。 (Nowadays many people use mobile payments, so fewer and fewer people carry wallets when going out.)

9. 呢個名牌銀包成千蚊，真係好貴呀！ (This brand-name wallet costs over a thousand dollars. It's really expensive!)

10. 佢打開個銀包，發現冇晒啲現金，即刻報警。 (He opened his wallet and found all the cash was gone, so he called the police immediately.) [end of text]


